From 42a7e8affd417f476e839c682a3b44340a9a171d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:10:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Node machine: the fact words' kernel at reader time, its
 inputs from the front's records (#2850)

#2850's steps 1 and 2 made T's records from fact words in a kernel that ran
after the pipeline, on windows made from T's own columns and the walk's
nodes. A compile that skips the walk for an expression has neither.
measure-node-machine --shadow --front-facts runs the same kernel where #2524
put the machine: after T types a chunk's roots at reader time, each
expression T takes is appended to a batch's windows, and the batch is run
with T's records as the oracle, over poisoned records and over decoys, and
timed beside T on the same expressions.

A window's inputs are made twice. node_facts_append makes them from T's
columns, as after the pipeline. node_facts_front_expression makes them from
the lean front's records and the reader's columns alone: an operand a
distance back in the postorder, a leaf its declaration's line or a line of
its own, a member's name the token after the operator's, a cast's and a
return's type the reader's, a call's arguments by their subtrees' sizes. The
two are compared field for field, and the checked run takes the second. An
expression the front's records don't give whole (a chunk's end cut its
records) takes the first's and is counted.

The words at reader time: a type's row is made before the expression that
reads it is appended; a declaration's line at its first use; an enumerator's
value from the reader's own column (the input's list is made when the reader
ends), a value past 64 bits marked on its line (BUSTER_NODE_FACTS_HIGH) so
that its leaf is T's; a literal's line is a batch's own.

On the 9700X (docs/one-core-path.md, "Step 2's third piece"): every record
and every input exact on sqlite3.c, Lua, musl and the compiler's own source;
the kernel 15.8 TSC ticks a record where T takes 49.7 on the same
expressions; its inputs' making 29.5, a record at a time, and no faster by
passes over a batch. The piece's gate of 35 ticks with the inputs' making is
missed: the window's columns are the front's to write as it makes each
record, not a stage after it.

No compile runs any of it.

Part of #2850.

